uestion (B of the brief).** On a graph of pathwidth `k`, how many","+exact-size empty pairs are there (`X₁`), how many distinct separators","+among them (`X₂`), how many closed pairs of the forced sizes (`X₃`; and","+`X₃′`, the image of the exact-size pairs under the `A`-first closure of","+L2), and how many move-classes (`X₄`)? How fast do the ratios `X₁/X₂`,","+`X₁/X₃`, `X₁/X₄` grow with `n`, in nats per vertex, against the `0.066`","+that a `0.02` gain in `β` needs at `c = 10` (the pair exponent's slope at","+`β*` is `3.3` per unit of `β` there; `3.4, 3.9` at `c = 6, 4`;","+`rate_preview.log`)? Each ratio is what one representative count merges:","+`X₂` merges every pair with the same separator (the component flips of","+plan §0, and the reversal), `X₃` merges every pair with the same closure,","+`X₄` merges every pair reachable by single swaps.","+","+**The events counted, exactly.** `X₁` is the number of ordered pairs","+`(A, R)` with `|A| = t`, `|R| = N − t`, no `A–R` edge (the count of","+`FirstMoment.lean`). `X₂` is the number of distinct `S = V ∖ (A ∪ R)` over","+those pairs, which by L1′ (c) is the number of `k`-sets in `E_bip`. `X₃` is","+the number of ordered closed pairs with `|A| ≥ t`, `|R| ≥ N − t`,","+`|S| ≤ k` (§2.3; enumerated by the pruned search of","+`closed_pairs_pruned`, which agrees with the `2ⁿ` enumeration of","+`closed_pairs` on all 2,200 rows at `n ≤ 16`, `k = pw`). `X₄` is the","+number of connected components of the graph on exact-size pairs in which","+two pairs are adjacent when their labellings `V → {A, R, S}` differ on at","+most two vertices; at exact sizes a single vertex cannot change class, so","+an edge is exactly one swap of two vertices between two classes","+(`A ↔ S`, `R ↔ S` or `A ↔ R`). When `N` is even, `(R, A)` is an exact-size","+pair whenever `(A, R)` is, with the same `S`: the reversal is in `X₁` and","+not in `X₂`, and the parity split below separates it from everything else.","+","+### 3.1 Instances","+","+| source | cells | per cell | instances | exact value from |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| fresh `G(n, c/n)` | `n ∈ {14, 16, 18, 20, 22, 24}` × `c ∈ {4, 6, 8, 10}` | 200 | 4,800 | the C program `pathwidth_solver/cli/pathwidth -l -t 60` (every graph proved, `refutation` or `bound`; the layout kept in `instances.csv`); at `n ≤ 16` the subset DP `vertex_separation` agrees on all 1,600 |","+| pilot `G(20, c/20)` | `c ∈ {4, 6, 8, 10}` | 137 | 548 | on record (`gnp_pilot/results.csv`); the overlap check at one size |","+| certified covers, fixed generator | `n ∈ {10, 15, 20, 25}` × `d ∈ {4, 6}`, `m = n` | 150 | 1,200 | on record (`learning/data/ensemble/results.csv`, `pw = optimum − 1`); regenerated from seed; the DP agrees at `n ≤ 16` |","+","+Seeds of the fresh graphs: `crc32(\"sep03:{n}:{c}:{i}\")`, `i < 200`;","+generator `networkx.gnp_random_graph(n, c/n, seed)` as in the pilot.","+Nothing on record was re-solved. The counts are taken at","+`k = pw − 1, pw, pw + 1, pw + 2` on every instance (caps on the","+enumeration were never reached: no row is marked skipped). The whole run","+is **7 s** for the solves and **66 s** for the counts on 8 workers at nice 19","+(516 s of enumeration in total, about 0.15 core-hours against the 3","+budgeted; the one-minute load was below 2).","+","+### 3.2 The counts at `k = pw`","+","+Geometric means over the cell (every instance has `X₁ > 0` at `k = pw`, as","+L1 says). `X₁/X₂` and the others are geometric means of the per-instance","+ratios. (`cells.csv`; the medians and maxima are there too.)","+","+**Fresh `G(n, c/n)`:**","+","+| `c` | `n` | mean `pw/n` | `X₁` | `X₁/X₂` | `X₁/X₃` | `X₁/X₃′` | `X₁/X₄` | max `X₁/X₂` | max `X₁/X₃` | max `X₁/X₄` |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 4 | 14 | 0.310 | 18.8 | 1.82 | 1.55 | 1.55 | 2.15 | 8.4 | 7.4 | 200 |","+| 4 | 16 | 0.291 | 27.8 | 1.94 | 1.59 | 1.59 | 2.29 | 5.6 | 9.9 | 120 |","+| 4 | 18 | 0.280 | 32.1 | 1.81 | 1.54 | 1.54 | 2.02 | 6.3 | 10.2 | 44.5 |","+| 4 | 20 | 0.269 | 54.