ree with the fresh ones","+  (`pw` means within 0.1, `X₁` and the ratios within 10–20%).","+- **One separator carries, at the median, one pair — and its reverse.**","+  `X₁/X₂` is 1.4–2.0 on the graphs and 1.4–1.6 on the covers, and the","+  parity split shows what it is (`checks.log`): when `N` is odd (no","+  reversal) the ratio is **1.08, 1.14, 1.23, 1.57** at `c = 10, 8, 6, 4`","+  and **1.03–1.09** on the covers; when `N` is even it is **2.04, 2.05,","+  2.14, 2.43** and `2.0–2.04`. So beyond the reversal a separator merges","+  a factor of `1.03–1.6` of pairs, more on sparse graphs; `X₂ = X₁` outright","+  on 13–14% of the graphs and 29% of the covers. The maximum over 200","+  instances is 2.4–11.5.","+- **The closure merges a factor 1.3–1.6 on the graphs, 1.7–3.3 on the","+  covers**, and **`X₃′ = X₃` on every fresh and pilot graph at `k = pw`**","+  (99.8% of the covers): at the pathwidth, every closed pair of the forced","+  sizes is the closure of some exact-size pair, so the two counts of §2.3","+  remark (iv) are one count here. They separate at `pw + 2` (`X₃′ < X₃`","+  on 27–40% of instances), where the closed pairs that no exact-size","+  pair reaches appear.","+- **The move-classes merge a factor 1.4–2.5 on the graphs**, `X₄ = X₁` on","+  39% of the graphs (every pair alone in its class), and the maximum over","+  a cell is 7–200: the clusters a typical instance carries at `k = pw`","+  are small, and the large ones are rare instances.","+","+### 3.3 The rates","+","+OLS slope of the per-instance `log` against `n` at fixed `c` (fresh graphs,","+`n = 14–24`, 1,200 instances per `c`) and against `n` on the covers","+(`n = 10–25`, 600 per `d`), with its standard error; nats per vertex of","+`n`. (`slopes.csv`.)","+","+| source | `c` or `d` | `k` | slope `log X₁` | slope `log X₁/X₂` | slope `log X₁/X₃` | slope `log X₁/X₃′` | slope `log X₁/X₄` |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| fresh | 4 | `pw` | 0.127 ± 0.011 | 0.010 ± 0.003 | −0.003 ± 0.004 | −0.003 ± 0.004 | −0.001 ± 0.007 |","+| fresh | 6 | `pw` | 0.100 ± 0.010 | 0.004 ± 0.003 | 0.002 ± 0.004 | 0.002 ± 0.004 | 0.003 ± 0.005 |","+| fresh | 8 | `pw` | 0.100 ± 0.009 | 0.002 ± 0.003 | 0.002 ± 0.003 | 0.002 ± 0.003 | 0.003 ± 0.004 |","+| **fresh** | **10** | **`pw`** | 0.092 ± 0.008 | **0.000 ± 0.003** | **−0.003 ± 0.003** | −0.003 ± 0.003 | **−0.003 ± 0.004** |","+| cover | 4 | `pw` | 0.104 ± 0.007 | −0.006 ± 0.002 | 0.006 ± 0.005 | 0.006 ± 0.005 | 0.002 ± 0.006 |","+| cover | 6 | `pw` | 0.060 ± 0.007 | −0.000 ± 0.003 | −0.041 ± 0.005 | −0.041 ± 0.005 | −0.061 ± 0.005 |","+| fresh | 10 | `pw + 1` | 0.193 ± 0.006 | 0.001 ± 0.003 | 0.007 ± 0.002 | 0.005 ± 0.002 | −0.070 ± 0.006 |","+| fresh | 10 | `pw + 2` | 0.328 ± 0.004 | 0.005 ± 0.002 | 0.060 ± 0.002 | 0.038 ± 0.002 | −0.152 ± 0.007 |","+| fresh | 4 | `pw + 2` | 0.280 ± 0.007 | 0.015 ± 0.003 | 0.015 ± 0.003 | 0.014 ± 0.003 | −0.126 ± 0.010 |","+","+At `k = pw` **no ratio grows**: every slope of `log X₁/X₂`, `log X₁/X₃`,","+`log X₁/X₄` is within `0.01` of zero at every `c` and both `d`, and at","+`c = 10` the two the kill names are `0.000 ± 0.003` and `−0.003 ± 0.003`","+— more than twenty standard errors below `0.066`. In the conversion of the","+header, the separator and the closure merge **at most `0.01` nats per","+vertex, i.e. at most `0.003` in `β`** at these sizes, against the `0.02`","+the brief's kill asks for. The covers at `d = 6` show the closure and","+move-class ratios *falling* with `n` (the `n = 10` cell, `pw/n = 0.85`, is","+nearly complete and its forced sizes are 1–2, where everything closes to","+everything). At `k = pw + 2`, with 100× more pairs, the closure merges","+more as `n` grows (`0.06` per vertex at `c = 10`, `0.04` for the image","+`X₃′`) while the move-classes multiply *faster* than the pairs (`−0.15`):","+abundant pairs fragment into many small classes rather than one fat one.","+These `pw + 2` rows are at a fixed offset, not a fixed `β`, and are not","+comparable across `n`